{"name":"Sauerkraut","hex":"#eee0b9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sauerkraut","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dish made by fermenting finely chopped cabbage.","A German person. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sauerkraut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sauerkraut","blocks":[{"text":"Sauerkraut is finely cut raw white cabbage that has been fermented by various lactic acid bacteria. It has a long shelf life and a distinctive sour flavor, both of which result from the lactic acid formed when the bacteria ferment the carbohydrates in the cabbage leaves."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauerkraut"},{"title":"Sauerkraut (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Sauerkraut is a German television series and a book"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauerkraut_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Kiszona_kapusta.JPG/500px-Kiszona_kapusta.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Kiszona_kapusta.JPG/500px-Kiszona_kapusta.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Polish kapusta kiszona","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKiszona_kapusta.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Saurkraut_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Saurkraut_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Saurkraut_%28cropped%29.JPG/1280px-Saurkraut_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Saurkraut_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Saurkraut_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Homemade sauerkraut","link":"https://en.